#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid "Lock screen"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid ""
"A photo on a screen or phone doesn’t fool Winky, screens look black in the "
"infrared image. An elaborately made printout or a mask could, just like with "
"Windows Hello without extra protection."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid "Unlock only with ✌"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid ""
"Your face alone is then not enough: the lock screen and the login after "
"startup also need your ✌. This protects you if someone holds the computer up "
"to your face, for example while you’re asleep or under pressure. Without a "
"✌, the password field appears after 8 seconds at most."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid "Login after startup"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid "Caution: the login keyring then stays locked"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid ""
"Your face also logs you in after a restart. The login keyring then stays "
"locked and asks for the password when a program needs it. Someone who looks "
"very much like you, or holds the computer up to your face, gets in without "
"the password from a switched-off computer too."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid "Also unlock the keyring (experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid ""
"Your login password is stored sealed in this computer’s TPM chip and handed "
"to the keyring only right after your face was recognized at the login "
"screen. Someone who has this computer may still be able to read it, for "
"example by starting it from a USB stick with Ubuntu or a related Linux; "
"without Secure Boot it’s even easier. Don’t use this password anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid "sudo in the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid ""
"A harmful program running as you can trigger a sudo request. But nothing "
"happens without your ✌, and every request shows up with the command. After "
"three unconfirmed requests, only the password works for 10 minutes."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid "Set up"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid "Administrator dialogs"
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid ""
"Password dialogs such as updates or installing software. The ✌ window shows "
"what you are approving. If one appears that you didn’t expect, don’t show "
"the ✌."
msgstr ""

#: src/app/gesicht_app.py
msgid ""
"Only KeePassXC 2.8 or later, installed as a normal package. Older versions "
"don’t have quick unlock on Linux, and the Flatpak version can’t register it "
"with the system."
